// Package domain — file types.go
//
// PURPOSE
//   Shared typed identifiers and small value objects used across more than one
//   aggregate in this bounded context. Per-aggregate types live in their own
//   file (see <entity>.go); this file is for the cross-cutting ones.
//
// THE SCOPING IDENTIFIER
//   Most multi-tenant systems scope every row to a tenant/org/workspace/account.
//   That scope is NOT passed as a bare ID through the layers — it travels inside
//   the *domain.Actor (see actor.go). What lives here is just the *typed ID* for
//   that scope, so the Actor and the repositories can reference it.
//
//   Questions to answer when you bootstrap the context:
//     - Is there a scoping entity at all?  (single-tenant internal tool → no:
//       delete TenantID, drop tenantID from Actor, drop it from repo SQL.)
//     - What is it called in your ubiquitous language?  (Tenant? Organization?
//       Workspace? Account? Project?) — rename TenantID → OrgID/WorkspaceID/… and
//       the constructor with it.
//     - Is it a UUID you mint, or an external id (Stripe customer, Auth0 org)?
//       If external, drop NewTenantID and let it be assigned from outside.
package domain

import "github.com/google/uuid"

// TenantID is the typed identifier of the scoping entity. Rename it to match
// your ubiquitous language; delete it (and the tenantID field on Actor) if the
// system is single-tenant.
//
// Format: UUIDv7 as string — time-ordered, so natural DB sort order matches
// creation order (better index locality than UUIDv4, no extra created_at sort).
type TenantID string

// NewTenantID generates a new time-ordered UUIDv7 TenantID. Delete this if the
// scope id comes from an external system rather than being minted here.
func NewTenantID() TenantID {
	return TenantID(uuid.Must(uuid.NewV7()).String())
}
